@startuml mate_agent_service_responsibility_boundary
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java.
' Observed behavior: the CampusClaw internal HTTP POST returns execution-scoped SSE without a public WebSocket path.
' Pending implementation design: the mate-service public HTTP contract and its SSE projection are not implemented in this repository.
' Architecture change: both hops use HTTP request-response, message responses stream SSE; Runtime Builtin commands return JSON.
' Product constraint: the UI receives chatId only; sessionId remains an internal Runtime identifier.
' Security hardening: mate-service terminates public auth and projects internal events instead of forwarding bytes transparently.
' Design reason: keep user-facing Chat lifecycle separate from durable Runtime Session identity and execution.
' Layout-only update: public and internal contract details remain owned by their design topics.
title HTTP Service Boundaries: Chat Identity, Session Execution
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 35
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #94A3B8
rectangle "Agent UI\nchatId and public events" as UI #EFF6FF
rectangle "mate-service\nPublic HTTP / authentication\nChat identity and event projection\nGuardrails and orchestration" as Mate #FFF7ED
rectangle "CampusClaw\nInternal HTTP / Session lifecycle\nAgent, Model, Context and Tools\nCurrent-branch Entries" as Runtime #ECFDF5
database "Mate Chat Store\nChat-to-Session association\nOwnership and product state" as MateStore #FFF7ED
database "RuntimeSessionStore\nSession configuration and state\nEntries and internal execution state" as RuntimeStore #ECFDF5
UI <--> Mate : Public HTTP\nJSON or request-scoped SSE
Mate <--> Runtime : Internal HTTP + request context\nResultBean / 204 / scoped SSE
Mate --> MateStore : owns
Runtime --> RuntimeStore : owns
MateStore -[hidden]down- RuntimeStore
legend bottom left
Public and internal hops have independent identities, VOs, errors, and event contracts.
Mate projects events; it does not forward Runtime bytes or sessionId to the browser.
Runtime receives request context without adding end-user credential checks.
Message / Skill executions stream SSE; Runtime Builtin commands return JSON.
Interrupt and confirmation each use a new Events POST. No current FollowUp queue.
Exact public paths and projection remain owned by the public Chat API design.
endlegend
@enduml
